The desk's original “one issue, one fix” conclusion does not match its own computed views.
This review uses the supplied support export dated 4 October 2026, not a live ticket-system query.
The review date records when we read the export; it does not make the exported reports current.

<EngineeringUpdate />

<IncidentReview />

## Recomputed cause table

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

The table deduplicates by report ID, then looks up each tenant's locale and booking form.
`Intl.DateTimeFormat(...).formatToParts` determines whether that locale is day first.
`causes.ts` assigns `hint` only for a day-first tenant using the form channel through
`booking-v3`; the other day-first paths are assigned `parser`.
`meta.browserLocale` and `meta.intakeTag` describe intake's guess, not a reliable cause.
If a tenant is missing or the mechanism is unverified, investigate instead of forcing a match.

## Received and merged are different clocks

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Change triage across the support desk

Matching subjects can suggest candidates, but cannot establish duplicates. The same cause
may have different subjects, and the same subject may describe different causes. Read the
body, tenant locale, form version, channel and reproducible behavior before merging.
Apply this to every product handled by this desk, not only `sched-prod`.

<DedupeExplorer />

Follow [current triage](/kb/triage/dedupe/) and [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/). The accepted
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) is preserved as the historical record.
The old triage guidance was reviewed in June 2024, beyond the shared layout's configured
review threshold; an accepted label did not make that advice current. The active page is now updated.

## While the desk keeps working

Current guidance stops automatic subject-only merges and routes new date reports by the two
mechanisms above, with an explicit investigation queue when the evidence is insufficient.
Keep unique report IDs and received/merged times with each ticket; transfer each report once
when splitting #4471. Track the unresolved timing reports as follow-up evidence rather than
silently subtracting them from the current classifier totals. The updated triage page uses
the new decision; refresh counts from the next export and have the desk owner review incoming exceptions.
The subsequent engineering update records different outcomes: parser fixed, hint won't fix after
the form's retirement. Preserve that difference in the ticket closure reasons.

## Evidence and limits

- Reports: `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`; last occurrence of an ID wins, as in `uniqueById`.
- Tenant configuration: `src/lib/data/tenants/*.json`; no manual list of day-first locales.
- Classifier and notes: `causes.ts`, `locales.ts`, `desk-notes.json`.
- Rendered evidence: `CauseTable`, `QueueTimeline`, `DedupeExplorer` and this page's computed review.
- We ran the supplied classification and rendered the kb. We have not run the production booking system or verified a production fix.

